# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transition guard for the move to home/ (.chezmoiroot)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# chezmoi's source root is now home/ (see .chezmoiroot), so this file is
# normally never read. It only matters for the ONE `chezmoi update` on a
# machine still running the old layout: that run pulls the new commits but
# applies them using the old root (the repo root). Without this guard it
# would create ~/home, ~/docs and ~/README.md. With it, that run is a no-op
# and the next `chezmoi apply` uses home/ correctly.
#
# Safe to delete once every machine has applied the new layout.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
README.md
docs
home
